# Copy to backend/.env and fill in real values. Never commit .env.
#
# backend/.env is loaded automatically by both `go run ./cmd/api` and
# `go run ./cmd/adk-playground`. Variables already set in your shell take
# precedence over this file, so a one-off override still works:
#
#   MCDVOICE_LIVE=0 go run ./cmd/api
#
# Syntax: KEY=value, quotes optional, `export` tolerated, # starts a comment
# (a trailing comment needs a space before the #).

# --- Gemini (required) ------------------------------------------------------
# Free key from https://aistudio.google.com/apikey
GOOGLE_API_KEY=your-api-key-here

# Model override. Defaults to gemini-3.5-flash, which is the newest Flash that
# answers reliably on the free tier: gemini-2.5-flash 404s for keys created
# after its deprecation, and 3.7/3.8-flash frequently return 503.
# GEMINI_MODEL=gemini-3.5-flash

# --- McDonald's Receipt Surveyer (Module 1) ---------------------------------
# MCDVOICE_LIVE=1 really completes the survey at mcdvoice.com and returns a
# usable validation code. Each run is irreversible and consumes the single use
# of a real receipt code, so leave it off while developing the agent.
# MCDVOICE_LIVE=0

# Your standing satisfaction rating, 1-5, submitted when the request does not
# specify one. Defaults to 5.
# MCDVOICE_RATING=5

# Dump each survey page's form controls to stderr. Use this on the first live
# run to capture the real question wording.
# MCDVOICE_DEBUG=0

# --- HTTP API ---------------------------------------------------------------
# PORT=8080
# CORS_ALLOWED_ORIGINS=http://localhost:5173

# --- Database (optional) ----------------------------------------------------
# Omit entirely to run with the in-memory store instead of Postgres. Agent run
# history then lives in memory and is lost on restart.
#
# Local Docker Postgres:
# DATABASE_URL=postgres://app:app@localhost:5432/app?sslmode=disable
#
# Neon: use the POOLED endpoint here (the host contains "-pooler"). sslmode is
# mandatory. connect_timeout covers the cold start when a suspended compute
# wakes.
# DATABASE_URL=postgres://USER:PASSWORD@ep-xxxx-pooler.us-west-2.aws.neon.tech/neondb?sslmode=require&connect_timeout=10
#
# Run MIGRATIONS against the DIRECT endpoint instead (no "-pooler"). Neon's
# pooler runs PgBouncer in transaction mode, which does not support
# session-level advisory locks, so migration tools cannot take their lock:
#   goose -dir backend/migrations postgres "$NEON_DIRECT_URL" up
#
# Pool sizing, idle time and health-check period are set in cmd/api/main.go but
# only when absent here, so pool_max_conns / pool_max_conn_idle_time /
# pool_health_check_period in this URL win if you set them.
